  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our two completed experiments (config_020 and config_032) establish that multimodal + multiprofile + scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted achieves ~52% accuracy, with weighted fusion slightly outperforming concat. However, we have no information about whether the RNA encoder choice (scgpt vs. scvi_n200) matters, which is a major architectural decision. Question: config_012 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable swap from our best result (config_032), changing only the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200. This directly tests whether a VAE-based latent representation can match or exceed the generative scgpt encoder in the multimodal fusion pipeline. Why best next experiment: With 7 experiments remaining, resolving the RNA encoder question early is critical—if scvi_n200 is competitive, it opens a large sub-space of configurations; if scgpt is clearly superior, we can focus remaining budget on optimizing around scgpt (e.g., image encoder, aggregation). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

